If a patient has a prescribed-opioid and has a prescribed-opioid-nonuse and at least 2 negative-tests verify the prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a confirmatory-test verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a clinician verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse then the clinician may discontinue the prescribed-opioid without an opioid-taper and may discuss a safe-unused-opioid-disposal-option with the patient.
If a patient has a prescribed-opioid and has a prescribed-opioid-nonuse and at least 2 negative-tests verify the prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a confirmatory-test verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse then the patient does not require an opioid-taper.
